 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No flood, water, animals or people drawn: an hourglass for «حتى إذا جاء أمرنا», the ship as a symbol for «احمل فيها». 40:1-4 and 40:20-21 are not glossed (first-person paraphrase of Allah; «احمل فيها» echo). STAGING v4: The plain town by day, the ark already built. Nuh is a blue drop labelled Nuh; the few who believed with him are three figures in light robes (a small group, no number is meant: the two tafsirs give none). Allah's command and His words to Nuh (40:1-21) keep the background quiet. An hourglass for when Our command came (40:1-4); the gushing of water from the oven is only a water-drop plate (40:5-6, Al-Muyassar: the sign of the coming punishment); no flood, rain, oven or animal is drawn (the pairs of every kind are not drawn). Nuh moves to the ark on 40:8 (carry in it). His family is not drawn (it includes women, and his son and his wife are the exception, never drawn): only a footsteps plate on 40:14. The believers walk to the ark on 40:21 (and whoever believed), and the camera holds on them for except a few (40:25). Nobody is drowned; nobody faces an empty side."
